      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-23T19:51:27.000Z",
      "title": "Final dividend of ₹8.00 announced",
      "body": "Shareholders will receive a dividend of ₹8.00. Ex-date: 27th May 2026 Payment date: 29th July 2026 Dividend yield will be 4.8%, which is lower than the industry average of 6.0%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by earnings (88% earnings payout ratio) but not covered by cash flows (112% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 13% per year over the past 10 years and has been stable with no material reductions to payments, indicating a long track record of dividend growth and stability. EPS is expected to grow by 12% over the next 3 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "3e455885-e9f0-4ea9-bf71-f7fd81b1e560",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-22T11:34:43.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS in line with expectations, revenues disappoint",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹16.52 (up from ₹15.78 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹788.7b (up 4.7% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹206.9b (up 4.9% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 26% (in line with FY 2025). Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.8%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 3.2% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 5.5% growth forecast for the Tobacco industry in Asia. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 1% per year but the company’s share price has fallen by 12% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings.",
